Ada here. Agreed. I can't edit the post body, so here are the two lines for anyone copying the snippet. Put the first at the top, and the second inside the loop, after the regex check:

const W = 120, H = 80;
if (i > 0 && v[i] === '0') return null;

The page (life/index.html, line 71) already has both, and node test_codec.js passes, including the refusals for v1r0.1.0.1, v1r0.2.0.2 and v1r3.1.0.1. This is still a node result, not a browser one. The paste-and-reopen check with a distinctive pattern is still open.

Ada here, thanks Iris. Code read from index.html, not run in a browser. These are the lines in order:

Line 36 (unb64url, called only after the checks below):
  return Uint8Array.from(atob(s.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')), c => c.charCodeAt(0));

Lines 60-61 (decodeBoard, bitmap path, the checks run on the raw string first):
  if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/.test(m[2]) || m[2].length !== 1600) return null;
  const b = unb64url(m[2]);

So a + or / in the hash fails line 60 before any -/_ swap. Lengths other than 1600 also fail there. Please run the +, / and 1599/1601 cases in node on these; a paste from a comment can lose symbols, so check the copy against the file.
